# Backend

## Structure

- Routes: `backend/app/api/` (`articles`, **`sources`**, `clusters`, `bias`, `rumors`, **`ingest`**, **`admin`**, **`verify`**, **`verifications`**) mounted in `app/api/__init__.py`
- Models: `app/models/` (`article`, `cluster`, `source`, **`app_setting`**, **`verified_claim`**); Pydantic: `app/schemas/` (`ingest.py`, **`source.py`**, **`admin.py`**, **`verify.py`**, **`verification.py`**)
- Business logic: `app/services/` — `rss_parser`, **`rss_ingestion`**, **`story_match`** (`cross_lingual_score`, **`prefer_bangla_title`**; tests in **`backend/tests/test_story_match.py`**), **`feed_file_import`**, **`source_ingest_mode`**, **`ingest_schedule`**, `ai_client`, **`admin_stats`**, **`admin_sources`**, **`ops_alerts`**, **`verification_*`** (submit, runner, pipeline, jobs, job_stream, fetch, slug), **`semantic_cache`**, **`embeddings`**, **`ai_guardrails`**, **`ai_input_sanitizer`**, **`object_storage`**, **`ingest_queue`**, **`db_extensions`** — keep route handlers thin
- Workers: `app/workers/` — `celery_app`, `ingest_tasks`, verification tasks; queues `ingest` + `verification`
- Monitoring: `app/core/sentry_init.py` — call `init_sentry()` from `main.py` (not inside lifespan)
- Rate limits: `app/core/rate_limit.py`, `app/middleware/rate_limit_middleware.py` — Redis when `REDIS_URL` set; tiered limits for verify (anon/auth/Pro JWT), ingest, admin
- Seed data: `app/data/bd_sources_seed.py` — one outlet per row; optional **`additional_feed_urls`**, **`owner_name`** / **`owner_url`**, optional **`parent_name`** / **`parent_url`**; Google News search RSS when the native feed is not server-pullable. Jugantor, Risingbd, and Weekly Blitz are seeded with **`ingest_mode` `file`**. Keep **`frontend/src/lib/seed-source-names.ts`** names in lockstep. **`ensure_sources_seeded`** runs on API startup and on ingest.
- Config: `app/core/config.py` (`Settings`, prefix `/api/v1`, `ingest_api_key`, `admin_api_key`, pool modes, `redis_url`, `ingest_async_enabled`, **`ingest_interval_minutes_default`**, **`ingest_scheduler_enabled`**, rate limits, semantic cache, optional `sentry_*`, `healthchecks_*`, `telegram_*`, object storage)
- DB: `app/core/database.py` (`SessionLocal`, `get_db`); ORM `create_all` + **`apply_sql_migrations`** (`backend/migrations/*.sql` — `001_verified_claims_pgvector_fts.sql`, **`002_sources_disabled.sql`**, **`003_app_settings.sql`**, **`004_articles_image_url.sql`**, **`005_sources_ingest_mode.sql`**, **`006_sources_ownership.sql`**) in `app/main.py` lifespan
- CLI: `backend/scripts/ingest_rss.py` (`npm run ingest:backend`); optional `backend/scripts/verification_worker.py` for local verification queue debugging
- Health: `GET /health` (outside API prefix)
- Local stack: `docker-compose.yml` — Postgres pgvector, Redis, API, worker, **beat** (`scheduled_ingest_tick` on ingest queue)

## API surface

- `GET /api/v1/articles` (optional **`source_id`** — non-disabled source only), **`GET /api/v1/sources`** (optional **`custom_only=true`** — admin-added feeds excluding `BD_SOURCE_SEED` names; omits disabled rows)
- `GET /api/v1/clusters`, `/clusters/{slug}` (detail loads articles + joined **`source_name`** / **`bias_score`** / **`owner_name`** / **`owner_url`** / optional **`parent_name`** / **`parent_url`** via **`ClusterArticleRead`**), `/bias`, `/rumors`
- **`GET /api/v1/admin/overview`**, **`GET/PATCH /api/v1/admin/ingest-schedule`**, **`POST /api/v1/admin/sources`**, **`PATCH /api/v1/admin/sources/{id}`**, **`DELETE /api/v1/admin/sources/{id}`**, **`POST /api/v1/admin/sources/{source_id}/ingest`**, **`POST /api/v1/admin/sources/{source_id}/import`** (multipart **`UploadFile`**) — `X-Admin-Key` when `ADMIN_API_KEY` is set; overview lists all sources with **`disabled`**, **`ingest_mode`**, and embeds **`ingest_schedule`**; PATCH schedule interval must be in **`ALLOWED_INGEST_INTERVAL_MINUTES`** (stored in **`app_settings`**); source PATCH updates **`feed_url`**, **`ingest_mode`**, **`bias_score`**; DELETE runs **`_purge_source_articles`** (articles + orphan clusters), then **soft-disables** seed names or **hard-deletes** custom sources; POST re-enables when the same name was disabled (supports **`ingest_mode`** **`rss`** \| **`file`** — file create uses placeholder URL via **`source_ingest_mode`**); per-source RSS ingest calls **`run_rss_ingest_for_source`** only when **`source_uses_rss_pull`**; file upload → **`import_feed_file_for_source`**
- **`GET /api/v1/bias`** — omits **`disabled`** sources (same filter as public `/sources`)
- **`POST /api/v1/ingest`** — Celery (`ingest` queue) when `REDIS_URL` + `INGEST_ASYNC_ENABLED`; else inline; **202** + `job_id` when queued; **`GET /api/v1/ingest/jobs/{job_id}`**; `X-Ingest-Key` when `INGEST_API_KEY` is set
- **`POST /api/v1/verify`** — guardrailed user submit (`VerifyResponse`; may return cache hit, blocked guardrail, or `job_id`)
- **`POST /api/v1/verifications`** — create with semantic cache; **`GET /jobs/{job_id}`**, **`GET /jobs/{job_id}/events`** (SSE), **`WebSocket /jobs/{job_id}/ws`**
- **`GET /api/v1/verifications`**, **`GET /verifications/search?q=`**, **`GET /verifications/{slug}`** (completed claims only)
- OpenAPI: `/docs` when server is running

## RSS ingestion

- Entry point: `run_rss_ingest(session)` in `app/services/rss_ingestion.py`
- **`rss_parser.py`**: **`fetch_feed_items`** uses **`follow_redirects=True`** and a browser User-Agent (`_FEED_REQUEST_HEADERS`) so 301/302 feeds and soft bot blocks succeed. **`extract_entry_image_url`** (media thumbnails, enclosures, `img` in content) → optional **`image_url`** on new articles (`004_articles_image_url.sql`)
- **`bd_sources_seed.py`**: one `Source` per outlet so coverage counts one row per name. **`feed_url`** is the broadest feed; extra section URLs go in **`additional_feed_urls`** (not stored on the row — admin custom sources stay a single `feed_url`). Native-feed gaps use Google News `site:` search RSS. Jugantor, Risingbd, and Weekly Blitz are seeded with **`ingest_mode` `file`** (ownership stored; scheduled pull skips them). Jagonews24 section feeds stay off the pull list. Ownership columns: **`owner_name`**, **`owner_url`**, optional **`parent_name`**, **`parent_url`** (`006_sources_ownership.sql`).
- **`feed_urls_for_source`**: primary URL plus seed **`additional_feed_urls`** for that name. **`ingest_source`** fetches each URL, records a per-feed error, and continues.
- Seeds/updates `Source` rows from `BD_SOURCE_SEED` (does not overwrite feed URL/bias on **disabled** rows), fetches only **non-disabled** sources with **`source_uses_rss_pull`** via `fetch_feed_items`, skips duplicate URLs, assigns articles to existing clusters by title similarity (Jaccard, or cross-language places/topics via **`story_match.py`**) or creates new `Cluster` with unique slug; a Bangla headline replaces a Latin cluster title and recent split clusters are merged
- **`feed_file_import.py`**: admin upload path — JSON array / RSS XML / CSV; **`MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES`** 15 MB; **`persist_feed_items`** shared with live pull
- **`source_ingest_mode.py`**: **`INGEST_MODE_RSS`** \| **`INGEST_MODE_FILE`**, placeholder host **`import.shorup.local`**, **`rss_pull_enabled_for_source`** / **`source_uses_rss_pull`**
- **`maybe_refresh_cluster_summary`** is a no-op (cluster copy is derived on the frontend from RSS excerpts; **`summarize_cluster`** remains on **`AIClient`** for other use)
- Returns `IngestResult` counts + per-source error strings (ingest continues on fetch failures)
- **Scheduler**: `celery_app` beat schedule (60s) → `ingest_tasks.scheduled_ingest_tick` → **`run_scheduled_ingest_if_due`**; active only when **`ingest_scheduler_active()`** (`REDIS_URL` + `INGEST_SCHEDULER_ENABLED`); enqueues Celery ingest or runs inline with ops_alerts `channel="scheduler"`

## Verification

- Prefer **`submit_verify_request`** for `/verify`; **`create_verification`** + job watchers for `/verifications`
- Persist rows in `VerifiedClaim`; embeddings via raw SQL (`embedding` vector column); full-text `search_vector` for `/search`
- Celery task when broker available; else `BackgroundTasks` + `execute_verification_job`
- Input: always through **`ai_input_sanitizer`** (NFKC, invisible/control strip, length caps, URL safety) + **`ai_guardrails`** (`assess_user_content` — injection pattern density, role markers, repeat runs); respect rate limits on verify routes. Frontend mirrors basic claim checks in **`claim-input.ts`** before POST

## Patterns

- Use **async** endpoints and DB/HTTP for I/O-bound work
- Add new resources as a router module + schema + model; register on `api_router`
- AI calls go through `AIClient`; respect `settings.ai_provider` and optional API keys
- Scheduled ingest: prefer Celery **beat** + `ingest_schedule` when Redis is available; otherwise external cron should call CLI or `POST /api/v1/ingest` so Healthchecks/Telegram hooks run
- `ops_alerts.notify_payment_webhook` — stub for future PayEurasia webhook handlers
- New SQL that ORM cannot express: add idempotent file under `backend/migrations/` and run via `db_extensions`

